<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  PLAYER header overflow (G1a).

  The frozen `Menu / Плеер` (2444:18763 light / 2444:18707 dark) is a 206x264
  surface with **four** rows, and their layer names say what they are: Найти
  трек, Таймер сна, Сообщить о проблеме, История эфира. Every label in the frame
  itself reads "Действие" - the rows are placeholders whose names are the design's
  only statement of intent.

  None of those four exists yet, and **Настройки is not among them**. It is here
  because the owner placed the Settings entry on this control: the frozen file
  never draws a path to `settings` at all (see docs/SETTINGS-APPEARANCE-3.6.6.md),
  so where it is reached from is a product decision rather than something the
  frame can settle. The four frozen rows arrive with the phases that build them,
  and this menu grows into that surface rather than replacing it.

  A platform PopupMenu, deliberately and temporarily - the same decision, for the
  same reason, that the COLLECTION overflow records: the frozen 206x264 r20 menu
  on `menu_surface` is its own piece of work, and relocating the action first
  keeps it reachable across the interval.
-->
<menu xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <item
        android:id="@+id/player_action_settings"
        android:title="@string/settings_title" />
</menu>
